    {
      "id": "seo-proof",
      "factory": "SeoProofBlock",
      "props": ["cms.proof (title, items[3])"],
      "status": "done",
      "wave": 8,
      "note": "Vertical-specific: HVAC equipment/maintenance/emergency; Snow trigger/SLA/compliance; Lawn programme/re-entry; Pool readings/swim-ready; Roofing inspection/report/project; Pest monitoring/guarantee; Health coordination/milestones/secure-docs (logistics only, no clinical claims); Beauty specialist/formulas/loyalty."
    },
    {
      "id": "seo-pricing",
      "factory": "SeoPricing",
      "props": ["cms.pricing (note, rows[] {name, from|null, unit|reason})"],
      "status": "done",
      "wave": 8,
      "note": "'from' prices come ONLY from CMS; from:null renders the needs-assessment variant. States: ready|loading|empty (empty = no published prices, quote-only copy). Wave 12 (Calm Harbor/Beauty): when the vertical supplies pimPricing, ready renders the repeated LIVE public PIM collection pim.pricing[] instead of cms.pricing.rows[] — public SPA_SERVICE + SPA_MEMBERSHIP items only (never SPA_RETAIL); each seo-pricing-row binds code/name/displayPrice/optional interval|shortDescription, carries data-product-code, and renders displayPrice VERBATIM (presentation never calculates, estimates, compares or transforms a price). empty truthfully states nothing is published — no quote, booking or fallback price. Section CTA stays honest navigation (auth.gotoSignin)."
    },
    {
      "id": "seo-pricing-row",
      "factory": "inline in SeoPricing",
      "props": ["pim.pricing[] (code, name, displayPrice, interval?, shortDescription?) OR cms.pricing.rows[i]"],
      "status": "done",
      "wave": 12,
      "note": "Stable row hook (data-module + data-visual-id seo-pricing-row). PIM rows carry data-product-code and data-bind=pim.pricing[]; legacy CMS rows keep data-bind=cms.pricing.rows[i]. Same accepted visual composition either way."
    },
    {
      "id": "seo-service-area",
      "factory": "SeoServiceArea",
      "props": ["cms.meta.serviceArea", "cms.area (cities[], note)"],
      "status": "done",
      "wave": 8,
      "note": "City/region chips + abstract coverage rings (deliberately schematic — no fake addresses/pins). Real map/polygon is a CMS media slot."
    },
